<title>THAILAND: Thai Jan-Sept petroleum demand up 10 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Thai Jan-Sept petroleum demand up 10 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's petroleum demand in the first nine months of 1996 rose by 10.1 percent to 882,480 barrels per day (bpd) from the same period last year, the Petroleum Authority of Thailand (PTT) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Consumption of refined products rose 10.4 percent to average 726,550 bpd while demand for natural gas went up by 8.7 percent from the same period last year to the equivalent of 155,930 bpd, PTT said in a statement.</p>
<p>Petroleum purchases in the first nine months of 1996 averaged 1,047,800 bpd, a 19.1 percent increase from the year ago period. Imports totalled 778,400 bpd--a 22.3 percent rise from the same period.</p>
<p>Procurement from local sources rose 10.8 percent to 269,400 bpd, the report said.</p>
